# psnes deterministic core build.
#
# The wasm artefact under frontend/static/psnes-core/ IS committed: the
# production image builds with `npm run build` and has no emscripten toolchain,
# so an ignored artefact means lockstep mode ships with a missing core. It is
# reproducible from a pinned snes9x commit - rerun core/build.sh and commit the
# result whenever core/src or the pin changes.
core/vendor/
core/.emcache/
core/build/
core/dist/
core/test/roms/

core/build/

# Superpowers scratch (brainstorm mockups, SDD ledger)
.superpowers/

# Claude Code
#
# Only the local, per-developer half is ignored -- NOT `.claude/` wholesale.
# Shared project config lives in the same directory (settings.json, commands/,
# agents/, skills/, hooks/) and is meant to be committed like any other config;
# ignoring the parent would hide it from review without anyone noticing.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.shot.mjs

# Dev TLS for the Quest. WebXR needs a secure context, and the headset reaches
# this machine by LAN IP rather than localhost, so `bun run dev` can serve
# self-signed HTTPS when VITE_HTTPS=1. Regenerate with the openssl.cnf in there;
# never commit the key.
frontend/.certs/
